  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Institutional Capacity of Druk Holding and Investments to Improve Corporate Governance in Bhutan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The task will seek to leverage additional trust fund resources to support support good governance practices, foment and strengthen corporate governance in Bhutan, via direct specialized training programs for company directors, and leadership for company boards in their efforts for improved transparency, effectiveness in governance, and accountability. Support would be provided to Druk Holding and Investments (DHI). DHI demonstrated   its commitment to improving corporate governance of SOEs in Bhutan through previous work with the IFC which helped finalize DHI&apos;s ownership policy.  The proposed IDF will build on this work, focussing on:  (1) a corporate governance code for DHI companies; (2) an institutional needs assessment for DHI companies; and (3) Awareness building and training to help the adoption of higher corporate governance standards in Bhutan.. The objective of this grant is to improve corporate governance among State Owned Enterprises (SOEs) in Bhutan. Specifically, the grant will technical assistance to Druk Holdings and Investment (DHI) for support to Corporate Governance capacity building within DHI by working with them to: &quot;&quot;   Develop corporate governance norms for DHI&apos;s portfolio companies, including -a corporate governance code for DHI portfolio companies (already started by DHI) &quot;&quot;   Conduct an institutional needs assessment of a number of DHI companies on &quot;&quot;    Raise awareness of corporate governance and build Capacity of DHI Companies via -conducting corporate governance workshops -Training trainers on corporate governance. The objective of this Grant is to improve Corporate Governance (CG) among State Owned Enterprises (SOEs) in Bhutan by providing technical assistance to Druk Holding and Investments (DHI) to support Corporate Governance capacity building.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
